> FILE(docs/drafts/reviews-2026-11-13/proxy-reg21-draft15-delta.md). G1: the record's commit adds the table's output file and its stderr file and nothing else; "before" means a strict ancestor of the record's commit, so a change in the record's own commit counts as after (a commit is its own ancestor in git); if REG-19's table is computed or read and no record is made, batch 2 is not computed, with that reason ("Batch 2 not computed"; also "What was known" and the stopping rule's bullet "Between batch 1 and batch 2"). G2 (the `docs/status.md` notice on the record and on REG-20's commits to the judged path) is due before batch 1 and is listed in the [DECISION] (delegate).
