> ### Changed because of the rule F review of draft 15 (round 10; its required item J1–J3; text only)
> FILE(docs/drafts/reviews-2026-11-13/rulef-reg21-draft15-r10.md). Made on draft 16 (draft 15 with the owner-proxy's G1, which this round did not see). J1: the cut is the UTC start time in the record's file name, and a change counts as before it only if its commit is a strict ancestor of the record's commit with a committer time earlier than the cut, so a record committed late no longer admits changes made after the table was read. J2: the record is the first saved stdout that holds the table; a run that raised printed none, and its files go in with `final.sh`'s [OPS] entry. J3: a run on which the seal skipped every REG-19 folder (empty `seeds_run`) is not REG-19's table. (b) compares against the seeds the record counts, its rows less `excluded` ("Batch 2 not computed"; hand duty (b)). Optional items taken: "the commits of this [REG] and of its delegate [DECISION]" ("What was known", the unread item); the time of batch 1, and of REG-22's batch 1, is the start time in its saved file's name, and an overrule counts as blind only if committed earlier ("What was known", the rule on the two batches; the batch-1 [RESULT]).
